      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During its heyday, Alexandria Bay’s main access was a steamer from Clayton, turning the village into a 19th‑century resort hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandria_Bay%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village’s single stoplight marks the junction of NY‑12 and NY‑26, the only traffic light in Alexandria Bay.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandria_Bay%2C_New_York",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Alexandria Bay sits on the south bank of the Saint Lawrence River, just a stone’s throw from the U.S.–Canada border.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandria_Bay%2C_New_York",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Since 1977, the Thousand Islands Bridge Authority has poured millions into restoring Boldt Castle and its surrounding structures.",
